+- (2k2, D2-109, D2-118) **Ignored by git:** `.telelean/runs/.gitignore` holds `/*` (written by `ensureRunsDir` when absent): every entry of the runs folder, itself included, and never a path below them, so the ripgrep that the CLI's Grep runs from ws/ inside the model's repository still searches ws/ (a bare `*` would hide all of it). `/.telelean/runs/` is one of Initialize's `.gitignore` lines. History's snapshots, Apply's writes, `graph.json` and the model's file listing never include anything under it.
+- (2k2, D2-122) **Ripgrep and the model's own ignore files:** each run folder holds a `.ignore` of `!*` (beside ws/, never inside it). Inside the model's git repository, the ripgrep that the CLI's Grep and Glob run from ws/ also applies the model's `.gitignore`, the user's global ignore and `.git/info/exclude` to paths below ws/, so a rule such as `Model/` would hide those files of ws/ from Grep while Read still sees them; a `.ignore` between ws/ and the repository outranks the ignore files above it, and `!*` restores what Grep saw when ws/ lay outside any repository.
+- (2k2, D2-110, D2-123) **Consent:** `.telelean/runs/consent.json`, `{ "format": "telelean-consent", "version": 1, "claude": true, "root": "<the folder's real path>" }`, written on a yes; only that exact content, for this very folder, counts. A clone never carries it (git-ignored), and neither does a copy, a move or a rename (the file names the folder it was written for, so a copy of the whole folder asks again, as U3 says); a recreated folder starts without it.
